    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e381173e_75002f3d",
        "filename": "acme/autocert/autocert.go",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 251,
      "author": {
        "id": 6347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-12T09:53:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah yes, good point. I think this one would have belonged to tokensMu because they are all used in the same authorization flow.\n\nBut, because apparently tls-sni challenges don\u0027t seem to be coming back, I removed \"If HTTPHandler is never called, the Manager will only use TLS SNI\" part. Let\u0027s try \"http-01\" unconditionally. If we can\u0027t get port 80 requests, so be it. It fails pretty fast anyway.\n\nEither way, I\u0027ll see about reducing the number of mutexes.",
      "parentUuid": "a9eae6a2_4fcb6bfe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 251,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 251,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "tag": "autogenerated:gerrit:newPatchSet",
      "revId": "0e3247d9797d99fea8011d1def1515ad37a803f8",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
